  Classification on Saliency4ASD via Multi-Stream Distillation."
  IEEE Open Journal of the Computer Society, 2026.
  https://doi.org/10.1109/OJCS.2026.3738736

Training data
  The ONNX models were trained on the Saliency4ASD dataset:
  H. Duan, G. Zhai, X. Min, Z. Che, Y. Fang, X. Yang, J. Gutiérrez,
  P. Le Callet. "A dataset of eye movements for the children with autism
  spectrum disorder." ACM Multimedia Systems Conference (MMSys), 2019.
  https://doi.org/10.1145/3304109.3325818
  Zenodo record 2647418, released under CC BY 4.0.
  Cite that paper when you use the models or the dataset.

Stimuli
  The 300 Saliency4ASD pictures come from the MIT1003 collection
  (T. Judd, K. Ehinger, F. Durand, A. Torralba. "Learning to predict where
  humans look." ICCV 2009, https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCV.2009.5459462).
  Their copyright stays with the original photographers. This repository and
  the published APKs do not contain them, and the Apache License does not
  apply to them. Users download the pictures from Zenodo themselves.

Pretrained weights
  The teacher and student backbones start from ImageNet weights distributed
  by timm (https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models, Apache-2.0).

